{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters","id":691410,"title":"Compact: Ride to Damascus - The Beastcrafters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-06T10:45:23-07:00","id":691410,"title":"Compact: Ride to Damascus - The Beastcrafters","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Ride to Damascus<br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The Beastcrafters</span></span></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <div align=\"center\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/wMlyScM.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">In 1961 a bus of Freedom Riders found themselves in an impossible situation. The crowd of racists that surrounded the bus grew thicker and thicker until the human wall became the pitch black walls of a tunnel. Onwards the bus drove towards a hellish red light and every soul on board heard either the sounds of a slave auction or cannibal drums from an Africa that never was. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But one man aboard was no man. Reverend Clarence Jackson was a Changeling and through his supernatural nature he knew that they had entered a story, a story with a moral: Fear that which is not like you for they are dangerous. As a Freedom Rider it need not be said what Clarence thought of this and his feelings about another story were even stronger. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Clarence remembered the ogre\u2019s beatings, and he remembered how the fear was so much worse than the pain. Most of all he remembered the ogre patiently explaining how this was for his own good. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">But Clarence was no longer a man, and his magic held a stronger dominion over stories. There were many good Christian tales with better morals that began when the Lord\u2019s believers found themselves in a land of peril. He rose to his feat and preached like he had never preached before. He preached of the Valley of the Shadow of Death, and of the Pilgrim's Progress. With his faerie magic he gave the story a twist, and the story became a Christian morality tale.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Jackson allowed the bus to arrive and he bid the riders to disembark so he could show them the truth. This hell held only one tormented soul. A figure so wrapped in shadows and chains that none could tell if it were a man or woman, white or black. \u201cBehold\u201d preached the reverend, \u201cThis poor soul was once victim of violence, and that violence inflicted a disease called hatred. Now he lies here in hell, his own hatred is the demons that torment him. But what power has hate compared to our Lord who is love and who is forgiveness.\u201d he turned to the horror \u201cSo I say onto you, forgive those who have transgressed against you and free yourself from this eternal torment!\u201d</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">With those words Clarence unleashed his faerie magic. The chains shattered, the shadows became light and gold, and then the hell just faded away leaving the Freedom Riders standing outside their bus on a deserted interstate. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">From there they went their separate ways. Reverend Clarence used his magic to turn invisible and escape the inevitable questioning. Deciding that this event was far too close to his own slavery for comfort he returned North to live a life free from conflict. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Convinced that she had experienced a genuine religious revelation a woman named Caitlin Lawson published her experiences accurately, save for the honest mistake of casting Clarence as an angel in mortal guise, and published it first as a successful work of short fiction under the name \u201cRide to Damascus\u201d, first in civil rights newsletters and then in an anthology of fiction. She remained an activist until 1965 whereupon she became a nun. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">While no Hunters were formed that day, many passengers took up the vigil in the weeks and months to follow after some time to think. They used Julia\u2019s story, and unpublished details, as a code to identify each other and form their own Cell.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Civil Rights movement was a turbulent time for the Vigil and occult knowledge flowed freely. After many contradictory and confusing explanations from witches, shaman, hunters and more the Cell\u2019s search took them to a Goblin Market. There they found a tutor for hire who agreed to teach them who Clarence Jackson was and how he performed his miracle. The Cell left the market with renewed purpose and a book containing the secrets of Talecrafting. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Price was high. Not one member of the cell lived to see the Civil Rights Act passed into law, but by the time the last founder died they had already trained twice as many students. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">[Picture: An elderly African American woman in traditional dress sits on an armchair surrounded by books. She is reading a thick leather tome with a picture of two faeries dressed and posed like the Brothers Grimm on the front.]</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fear leads to hatred. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Hatred leads to the dark side. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Enemy</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Like Clarence Jackson, half of Ride to Damascus\u2019s founding members, the half descended from Africans, saw fear as the tool of their oppressors; but even they don\u2019t consider fear the enemy. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beasts inflict fear yes, but terrible as it is, a Beast\u2019s hunger is less damaging than a vampire\u2019s thirst or the more omnipresent fears inflicted by one\u2019s fellow man. It\u2019s not fear that\u2019s the problem, it\u2019s the Beast\u2019s lessons. Lessons from mankinds savage and brutal past, lessons that have no place in the modern world. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">And so, Ride to Damascus use the power of Talecrafting to drag primordial Horrors into the modern world. They identify the monster\u2019s legend and enter it\u2019s Lairs, but they do so while invoking modern tropes and recraft the legend into a modern story with a modern lesson. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">To the Beasts this is an act of violence, the wilful destruction of their identity. To Ride to Damascus it\u2019s an act of violence as justified as any stake through a murderous Vampire\u2019s heart. It\u2019s the defence of the Beast\u2019s victims, and her victim\u2019s victims, and her victim\u2019s victim\u2019s victims. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">Stereotypes</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ageis Kai Doru: When we brought our Book the merchant\u2019s final words were \u201cdon\u2019t let The Greek see it\u201d. I have no doubt he told some form of truth and I\u2019ve read enough stories to know you do not ignore a warning like that, but that doesn't mean I have to like it.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Long Night: Reverend Clarence himself was both a faerie and a devout Christian. To their credit the Long Night do not see any contradiction, but they can\u2019t understand that faerie magic can be used for good. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ashwood Abbey: Our prey come from the depths of the human soul, is it any surprise that we might see people like them in both nature and denemour? But they are humans and can be dealt with by human law. Focus on our true mission. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Llannerch Athrawon: Our little magic trick can\u2019t cure so called Heroes so we mostly avoid them. But I did see this one, I was tracking a particularly vicious dragon, when I saw this fat slob in a cape led around by his dick by someone dressed, I kid you not, like it was the 1930s. He ended up killing the dragon without causing any trouble, I wish I spoke to her when I had a chance. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tickets</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ride to Damascus has a narrow and focused mission, consequently they have a stronger ideological unity than many Compacts however they still have a division of labour. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tickets North</b> </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">have retired from active hunting due to injury, fear, or just \u201chaving no more fight in them\u201d. Those that haven\u2019t retried entirely serve the Compact as recruiters, trainers, and as storytellers who promote tropes useful for talecrafting. Ride to Damascus doesn\u2019t have any storytellers influential enough to make a difference, but it lets wounded veterans retain a sense of dignity. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free Specialty: Expression (Storytelling) </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tickets South</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are the Compact\u2019s muscle and scouts. They track down beasts, serve as bodyguards to the talecrafters and if necessary they\u2019ll cut a path to safety after a hunt gone bad.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free Specialty: Firearms (Shotgun) or Streetwise (Beasts)</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Tickets to Damascus</span></span></b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> are the heart and soul of the Compact. They\u2019re the talecrafters, and by convention they\u2019re usually the leaders of their cell. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Free Merit Dot: Status (Ride to Damascus) or Talecrafting</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Status</span></span></span></b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ride to Damascus gain Status by having other members vouch for them. Your own cell provide little, they are supposed to vouch for you after all, so helping out other cells with advice or support is the fastest way to rise. This system leads to a correlation between Status and age, as older successful hunters are credited by the cells they inspired or recruited back in the day; and as those cells recruit others and rise in status their word carries more weight. The unofficial leaders or elders of the Compact are all in their twilight years and tell stories of their days in the civil rights campaign. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">O: To use stories as a tool you must first know stories. Take the Morality Tales specialty under Expression or Occult. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OO: Talecrafting requires keen observation to identify the start of tropes that can be then pushed to completion. Take a dot in Trained Observer</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOO: Beasts might be the enemy, but they\u2019re the enemy within all mankind. To forget this and see the Beast as the hated other is to step off the righteous path. Take the Sympathetic Merit and do not forget to use it on friend and foe alike. At this level you\u2019re also trusted enough to learn that the Compact\u2019s power comes from an (eminently desirable and stealable) Relic and you may learn Talecrafting. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOOO: After so long manipulating the power of stories some of that magic rubs off on them. Take two dots of Striking Looks, like the heroes of the stories their inherent goodness is plain for all to see, whether they\u2019re truly good or not. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">OOOOO: Use your Composure as though it was Potency to resist a Beast\u2019s Nightmares and add Composure to any roll to resist the effects of a Beast\u2019s Lair Tilts, for example add it to your Perception roll (making the roll Wits + Composure + Composure) to see in a dimly lit Lair. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Endowment: Talecrafting (O - OOOOO)</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It quite literally cost the entire founding Cell their lives to make it happen; a Goblin Merchant sold the faerie\u2019s secret magic of Talecrafting to a young Cell which thus became a Compact. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Who can say what Fate or plot was behind such a momentous event? Ride to Damascus certainly cannot, but they use their powers with skill and enthusiasm. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Ride to Damascus use the rules for talecrafting in Swords at Dawn with the following modifications: </span></span><ul><li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They spend Willpower in place of Glamour.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They cannot force the Pattern by spending Willpower. They rig events or wait for them to happen naturally. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They cannot pull of a Reversal of Fate.</span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">They do not suffer Talecrafting addiction, mortals are just more resistant to madness than faeries. </span></span></li> <li><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Their dicepool is Talecrafting alone, however Ride to Damascus can Talecraft as a teamwork action. Secondary Actors roll Expression and may apply specialties relating to a genre of stories. Secondary Actors do not need dots in Talecrafting and take no penalty if they have no dots. </span></span></li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beastcrafting</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beastcrafting, also known as Legendcrafting or Laircrafting is using Talecrafting to rewrite a Beast\u2019s Legend, Hunger and personality.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Beast crafting begins with reforging the Lair. In turn, this begins by learning the locations of the Chambers and the stories behind how those places became the Beast's. If a Beast emerged from the shadows behind a drunken reveller in a dark alleyway; then Ride to Damascus must enact the beginning of a story that involves a drunk reveller, a figure emerging from the Shadows and of course it be enacted in the same dark alley that is now a Chamber. This is the Pattern.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Once they have enacted their Pattern they roll for the hook. Roll Talecrafting vs Lair. As always Ride to Damascus can roll as a Teamwork action with secondary actors rolling Expression.</span></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Dramatic Failure or the Beast wins with an Exceptional Success: The environment changes around the Cell until they're inside the Chamber. The Beast is instantly aware of the invasion and a Cruel Twist of Fate is poised to strike. The Cell are not aware that the attempt failed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Failure or the Beast wins. The environment changes around the Cell until they're inside the Chamber. The Beast is not aware of this invasion but may discover it through the normal ways. A Cruel Twist of Fate is poised to strike. The Cell are aware that the attempt failed.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Success and the Beast's roll is overcome. The environment changes around the Cell until they're inside the Chamber. The Beast is not aware of this invasion but may discover it through the normal ways. If the cell complete the story begun by their Pattern the Chamber is successfully Laircrafted. No Cruel Twist of Fate occurs.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Exceptional Success and the Beast's roll is overcome. The environment changes around the Cell until they're inside the Chamber. The Beast is not aware of this invasion, and if the Beast or the Horror uncovers it then until the Cell complete their story it can only enter that Chamber by adopting a role that fits the story. This most likely prevents it from using it's supernatural abilities or violence. No Cruel Twist of Fate occurs.</span></span></div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">If the Beast or it's Horror uncovers an attempt at Laircrafting in progress it is likely to object. The simplest way is to simply attack the Cell and attempt to prevent them from completing the story. If the Beast cannot do so, usually because the Cell rolled an Exceptional Success for the Hook, it can try to subvert the story in progress. Roll the Beast's Manipulation and add the Successes to the earlier Lair roll made to Contest the Cell. If the new combined total exceeds the Cell's then when the end of the story is reached the Chamber will not change and the Beast is once more free to act as it pleases. Storytellers are strongly encouraged to give modifiers to the roll based on roleplaying.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"color:#434343\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Effects of Beastcrafting</span></span></b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Chambers changed by Beastcrafting become pleasant safer places even for intruders and the Horror must spend either a point Satiety or one Willpower per crafted Chamber to attack anyone within. However the real effects happen when the Beast itself is affected.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Every two weeks measured from the last time a Chamber was recrafted one Chamber is freed from the effects of Laircrafting, however if over half of the Lair has been reworked then instead one more Lair will be reworked. The Heart is always last, and after the Heart the Horror itself is next. The Beast's Hunger, Legend, and Nightmares are all replaced with new wholesome traits that promote the positive morals Ride to Damascus approve of.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">There is also a faster but more dangerous way to Beastcraft: Targeting the horror directly. Within the Heart or anywhere after the Heart has been reforged the Horror itself can be targeted by Beastcrafting. By using a Pattern where a what appears to be a monster eventually turns out to be harmless and friendly Ride to Damascus can reforge a Beast all at once. The obvious drawback is that this requires contact with either the Beast or the Horror; and as there's a role in the story for a monster the Horror will have full access to its powers. Reverend Clarence used his faerie magic to chain the Beast until the Story's conclusion. Ride to Damascus usually use actual chains on the rare occasions they try things the fast way.<br /> <br /> Reforged Chambers never provide advantages to a Beast who's being his usual Beastly self. For example the Beast could not use a new Lair Trait like &quot;brightly lit&quot; to flood a brightly lit room unless he has a completely wholesome motive in fitting with the new story Ride to Damascus are creating. </span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 05-13-2022, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T10:47:54-07:00","id":691433,"title":"","content":"Ride to Damascus came from two sources.<br /> <br /> 1) While I'm very satisfied with <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Llannerch Athrawon I felt they failed at one of my goals when writing them - to write a rebuttal to teaching through fear. I try to keep my politics out of my homebrew and let individual storytellers interpret things but in this case it went too far. Llannerch Athrawon had a rebuttal but how would it ever come up in play if they rarely interact directly with the Beast or the Beast's victims? Ride to Damasucs have to express their rebuttal directly through their choice of story and occasional improvised storytelling duels with a Beast.<br /> <br /> 2) Discussions with PenDragon about how Princess and Beasts are thematic opposites. Much of Ride to Damascus is just me translating my Princess ideas into Hunter form. That's why Ride to Dmascus are one of the most moral compacts I wrote - just compare them to Llannerch Athrawon's manipulative behaviour against the mentally ill. And yes, Princess can Talecraft. The fae focused Z-Splat lets them do it at Inner Light 7.<br /> <br /> <br /> Llannerch Athrawon probably knew how to do Beastcrafting at one point. They might have owned the very same book that Ride to Damascus own. They'd totally steal it given a chance.<br /> <br /> I'm very strict about keeping Hunter as &quot;mortals defending mortals&quot;, having Reverend Clarence be a Changeling skirts that line. I felt that since Beast naturally portrays a positive crossover friendly view of Changeling-Beast relationships it was important to show the other side somewhere. It fit in nicely here. </span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> Hopfully I won't have to change too much once I see the 2E talecrafting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-15-2015, 05:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T17:39:23-07:00","id":691817,"title":"","content":"What if the Beast decides to cut it's losses and &quot;releases&quot; the affected Chambers?<br /> <br /> How does the Compact feel when someone compares Beastcrafting to brainwashing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T00:16:40-07:00","id":692085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=691817#post691817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the Beast decides to cut it's losses and &quot;releases&quot; the affected Chambers?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to say Beast's can't release the affected Chambers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=691817#post691817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Compact feel when someone compares Beastcrafting to brainwashing?</div> </div> </div> </div>How does The Union feel when someone compares staking a vampire to murder?<br /> <br /> This is covered under The Enemy. The Compact know that Beastcrafting is an act of violence, but they think it's justified to protect the Beast's victims just like The Union think staking a vampire and leaving them out for the sun is justified to protect the Vampire's victims.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T01:18:17-07:00","id":692135,"title":"","content":"Okay, maybe it's just because I never really liked the redirection of Beast, but I actually think that this &quot;empowered compact&quot; is pretty good.<br /> <br /> For one thing, it makes a lot of sense as a thematic contrast to Beasts, and is quite intimately intertwined with them. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Llannerch Athrawon is similarly strong, but held at a distance by virtue of their very set up - playing Llannerch Athrawon is more like playing The Old Men of Marduk using the Marduk Society as disposable WMDs than anything.<br /> <br /> For another, it's a nice example of Light Gray without being &quot;too White Hat&quot; for the World of Darkness. Why do I say this?<br /> <br /> For starters, the ideology of the Ride to Damascus is based on &quot;talecrafting for a happy ending&quot;. That opens up possibility to a lot of dissent and inner conflict as to what defines a &quot;proper&quot; use of talecrafting. For example, I can easily see zealous Christian beastcrafters who try to use talecrafting as a sort of extreme Hell House - defanging the horrors, but at the same time using them as tools in guiding people towards &quot;good Christian behavior&quot;.<br /> <br /> Secondly, alongside this implicit grayness, there's the fact that the compact is given a realistic presentation; their numbers are small, and focused, and talecrafting is powerful, but they don't always win. In all honesty, I think the Ride to Damascus probably has more of a positive effect on the Vigil in that they are more likely to subtly leak warnings about local horrors and to generally inspire people to take up the Vigil, if not necessarily as part of the Ride.<br /> <br /> Thirdly, the sheer moral ambiguity of their powers and plans keeps them firmly down in the mud. Seriously, Beastcrafting is literally <b>raping somebody's soul</b>. You are forcing your way into somebody's very essence and mutilating it, torturing and resculpting their heart, their mind and soul into a shape that the Damascans consider more acceptable. This is violation of a nature we don't even have <i>words</i> for, the sort of stuff you'd expect to see hard-core villains using. The only thing that keeps Damascans from being villains is that A: they have genuinely good intentions - which would still leave them, at best, as Well Intentioned Extremists, were it not for B: the creatures they are using this power on can legitimately be claimed as being worse. No matter how you shape it, Beasts are abominations that literally feed on the pain, suffering, sorrow, misery, despair and terror of humanity as a whole. It's violating to force such a change on them... yet, still, the results can be legitimately for the greater good.<br /> <br /> I <i>love</i> this. It really feels appropriate for the World of Darkness. On the one hand, you have people arguing that this makes the Damascans little better than those &quot;straight camps&quot; that Christians send their gay and trans kids to in order to try and force them to be normal. On the other hand, you have people arguing that this is truly the better option, both for the people around them and for people who'd otherwise have to die for what they are. And <i>both sides are <b>right</b></i>.<br /> <br /> That moral grayness, that slippery slope, that razor edge between good and evil, the looming possibility that those fighting against oppression may have become oppressors in turn... that';s the sort of thing that makes the World of Darkness feel right.<br /> <br /> If I have one complaint, it's that I don't agree with the assessment that Damascans should be immune to Talecrafting Addiction. Power <b>always</b> has a price in the WoD, and furthermore, the Damascans are mucking around with something they shouldn't. Talecrafting lets a person mess around with the very fabric of reality, twisting events to confer to your plan for them. That's <i>not</i> conducive to a person's sanity.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I think Damascans should be <i>more</i> likely to get addicted to Talecrafting than Changelings should. Changelings have the buffer of having a hole where their soul should be filled with the Wyrd already - humans who tap into the Wyrd are being exposed to all its raw power, naked and unshielded. It's the difference between giving street-grade crack to a straight-edged goody-goody who's never taken any drugs before and giving it to a hardcore junkie - who do you think is going to handle it better?</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:47:58-07:00","id":692860,"title":"","content":"still waiting for the variant Beasts created by the Ride :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:08:11-07:00","id":692865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692135#post692135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thirdly, the sheer moral ambiguity of their powers and plans keeps them firmly down in the mud. Seriously, Beastcrafting is literally <b>raping somebody's soul</b>. You are forcing your way into somebody's very essence and mutilating it, torturing and resculpting their heart, their mind and soul into a shape that the Damascans consider more acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div> Notice that this makes another thematic parallel - enforced cultural assimilation vs Beasts-as-oppressed-minorities.<br /> <br /> Mind you I'm not sure Beasts-as-oppressed-minorities actually existed outside the authors head, they struck me more like an activists' impression of the 1%, it's that dissonance that made me want to write a rebuttal. I don't know if the update fixes that, I only skimmed it a little.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692135#post692135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I have one complaint, it's that I don't agree with the assessment that Damascans should be immune to Talecrafting Addiction. Power <b>always</b> has a price in the WoD, and furthermore, the Damascans are mucking around with something they shouldn't. Talecrafting lets a person mess around with the very fabric of reality, twisting events to confer to your plan for them. That's <i>not</i> conducive to a person's sanity.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's two reasons I did that.<br /> <br /> 1) Is that I think Talecrafting addiction is too nasty a drawback. I have never seen anyone use Talecrafting, IMO Cruel Twists of Fate provide all the Drawback Talecrafting needs.<br /> 2) Talecrafting addiction is thematically inappropriate for Ride to Damascus. If they started to slip I'd say - well you know revolutions tend to turn into tyranny? like that. Tyrants could use Talecrafting but IMO they're no more (and no less) likely to be addicted to it than activists.<br /> <br /> Besides Endowments don't usually have a price. Relics, nope. Benediction, not by rules anyway. Rites of Denial, well donating a few thimbles of blood never hurt anyone. Now you might argue that the price is that you fight monsters - but Ride to Damascus also want you to risk your life by fighting monsters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-07-2015, 04:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T13:32:56-07:00","id":692872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692865#post692865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind you <b>I'm not sure Beasts-as-oppressed-minorities actually existed outside the authors head</b>, they struck me more like an activists' impression of the 1%, it's that dissonance that made me want to write a rebuttal. I don't know if the update fixes that, I only skimmed it a little.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think a fuller discussion of this warrants it's own thread, but this idea of what Beasts were <i>was </i>rebutted by Matt before the revisions were released. I think people looked at the loose comparison between Heroes and folks like MRAs or Gamergaters and inferred then that Beasts must be those that these groups opposed, which they evidenced in Onyx Path's choice to include sample characters that defy normative identities. Since they seem do that in <i>every </i>book, I think I'd caution against looking at that as substantiating the idea that Beasts are meant to be seen as oppressed minorities.<br /> <br /> I think within the scheme of this write-up for the Ride you can talk about cultural assimilation with regards to forcing Beasts to adhere to mortal morality I guess? <br /> <br /> As an aside, I'm a little confused by the timeline. I'm guessing you're meaning this origin to take place in 1961, but you've got a typo at the start saying 1991.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T14:06:10-07:00","id":692908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692872#post692872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think a fuller discussion of this warrants it's own thread</div> </div> </div> </div> Probably not even that; it's been discussed at length and length already (and I wouldn't want to annoy PenDragon; he's cool). I will say it's not just Heroes and non-normative identities that gave me that impression but I think I should leave it at that. If you're really interested in discussing it further we can take it to private messagse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692872#post692872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think within the scheme of this write-up for the Ride you can talk about cultural assimilation with regards to forcing Beasts to adhere to mortal morality I guess?</div> </div> </div> </div> In theory you could but in practice Ride to Damascus care more about making Beasts obey mortal morality than fit into mortal culture.<br /> <br /> At least, I think that's the answer. I wasn't clear entirely on what you meant by drawing a distinction between morality and culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692872#post692872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but you've got a typo at the start saying 1991.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not any more I don't <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T23:03:32-07:00","id":693499,"title":"","content":"Didn't say it last time, because I was in a rush but this is some really good stuff The Kings Raven. Just had a few questions, but you've hit most of them already. Still wondering on how they react to non-Beast monsters though.<br /> <br /> Edit: I see now that it wasn't in my last post despite my memory of typing it out...curses, foiled again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T01:05:07-07:00","id":693543,"title":"","content":"Interesting, although if I were to include a hunter group to defang beasts, I'd go with a more &quot;familiarity breeds contempt&quot; sort of thing, and have the group study beasts and then use name magic to remake them.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't reworking chambers like this effectively give the beast extra lair traits for travel and manifestation? <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh noes, you replaced my haunted castle with a field of flowers. Now I can go all nightmare on elm street by teleporting to and then manifesting my beast powers allowing me to eat people in places with pretty scenery.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T12:33:27-07:00","id":694140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=692860#post692860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">still waiting for the variant Beasts created by the Ride :P</div> </div> </div> </div>You're going to have a long wait I'm afraid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=693499#post693499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't say it last time, because I was in a rush but this is some really good stuff The Kings Raven. Just had a few questions, but you've hit most of them already. Still wondering on how they react to non-Beast monsters though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No idea I'm afraid. I didn't want to dilute their relationship with Beasts so I never thought about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=693543#post693543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Interesting, although if I were to include a hunter group to defang beasts, I'd go with a more &quot;familiarity breeds contempt&quot; sort of thing, and have the group study beasts and then use name magic to remake them.</div> </div> </div> </div> Write them up! There's no rule saying only me and LostLight can write Hunter groups <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=693543#post693543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Wouldn't reworking chambers like this effectively give the beast extra lair traits for travel and manifestation?</div> </div> </div> </div>If Beastcrafting ever gives a Beast an mechanical advantage at being their evil Beastly self; it's a bug in the rules and should be fixed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-08-2015, 05:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T13:57:22-07:00","id":694180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=694140#post694140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have a long wait I'm afraid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I knew it would be the answer, yet I had to ask :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-08T18:54:30-07:00","id":694432,"title":"","content":"Ironically; in the absence of these 'wholesome' Hungers, I'm wondering if the Beast would slowly slide back to one of the five or just Starve. The idea that, even with best of intentions and reworking the Horror, changing the feeding mechanism so drastically doesn't work that well. Like trying to get a lion to go vegetarian. Or what is happening to the <a href=\"http://www.latimes.com/science/sciencenow/la-sci-sn-giant-panda-bamboo-meat-20150519-story.html\" target=\"_blank\">pandas</a>. It is not that the Begotten doesn't try to live up to it's new Legend and 'nice' Hunger...its that it doesn't meet their needs.<br /> <br /> Added bonus: neither does their old Hunger. It has been changed after all.<br /> Welcome to the World of Darkness; watch as the primordial nightmares starve to death.<br /> <br /> Note this doesn't undermine the philosophy of the group; the beliefs are just as valid and it is not always immediately obvious. It's not like pandas starved to death in a generation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:11:39-07:00","id":694611,"title":"","content":"Nope. The new 'wholesome' Hungers work just fine.<br /> <br /> I'm philosophically opposed to saying that a PC Splat should be doing something but be unaware it isn't working. *cough* Keepers of the Source *cough*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T00:43:13-07:00","id":694638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=694140#post694140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're going to have a long wait I'm afraid <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />No idea I'm afraid. I didn't want to dilute their relationship with Beasts so I never thought about it.<br /> <br /> Write them up! There's no rule saying only me and LostLight can write Hunter groups <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> If Beastcrafting ever gives a Beast an mechanical advantage at being their evil Beastly self; it's a bug in the rules and should be fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div> Naw, I'm well aware that coming up with ideas is the easy part of writing. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for beasts benefiting from this, perhaps that's overstating things, but a beast could make lemonade out of their lemons here.<br /> <br /> Hunters rewrite the chamber of a mongolian death worm, turning the deadly desert filled with the bones of the dead into say a fun beach, or perhaps even going the extra mile and turning the chamber into a flower filled meadow.<br /> <br /> Well the mongolian death worm, logically, would then be able to manifest their horror's abilities at beaches or flower filled meadows or locations similar to them instead of locations like a desert. Considering the chambers as written have to have some thematic similarity, the beast might be more versatile at where they can manifest their abilities, depending on how fundamental the differences the hunters can achieve here. <br /> <br /> Saying that altered chambers don't provide new lair traits would fix that, and logically should deny the beast the use of any chamber specific lair trait that isn't valid anymore. <br /> <br /> The second thing is less advantageous, really, but since beasts can teleport to their chambers and to locations similar to it, but I guess that's not really much of an issue if you add that altered chambers don't provide new traits, then even if the mongolian death worm showed up at the beach or meadow to get its Tremors on, it won't actually be able to manifest much, unless the beach or meadow shares lair traits the beast already had, or if the beast alters the environment, but than that's something the mongolian death worm could have done before anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T08:06:42-07:00","id":694920,"title":"","content":"Is their any way a beast can reverse beastcrafting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:46:00-07:00","id":695042,"title":"","content":"Is there any way a Vampire can reverse death by sunlight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T09:49:13-07:00","id":695047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=695042#post695042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way a Vampire can reverse death by sunlight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they need a gallon drum of Crisco, three trained Corgis, and the playbook for the New England Patriots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T11:43:15-07:00","id":695211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=694611#post694611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. The new 'wholesome' Hungers work just fine.<br /> <br /> I'm philosophically opposed to saying that a PC Splat should be doing something but be unaware it isn't working. *cough* Keepers of the Source *cough*</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'll be the first person to admit I hate the Keepers of the Source, but I don't think you can quite lay this accusation at their feet.<br /> <br /> The whole idea behind the Keepers is that they feel pain from being near loci, and this pain intensifies to excruciating levels when near beings hosting Essence (werewolves, mages, some Ordo Dracul vampires). It's not really that unjustified that they'd form the opinion that Essence-hosts are doing <i>something</i> wrong, even if those with greater understanding of the setting's metaphysics know that they're completely misguided in their beliefs.<br /> <br /> From their perspective, which is the perspective of &quot;being around this asshole HURTS ME until they give up their stolen Mother Earth's Blood&quot;, they are succeeding when they force someone to stop tapping a locus or to expend their essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:21:24-07:00","id":695284,"title":"","content":"But the Keepers don't care they're being hurt. They care that mother Earth is being hurt, and well, she's not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T13:47:43-07:00","id":695327,"title":"","content":"Keepers of the Source argument again, ha? Let me just grab my popcorn *munch munch*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T16:08:30-07:00","id":695429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=695284#post695284\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the Keepers don't care they're being hurt. They care that mother Earth is being hurt, and well, she's not.</div> </div> </div> </div>You know that. I know that. But, in universe? <b>They</b> don't know that. They're interpreting reality through what they sense, and even if it's factually wrong, it's still understandable that they <i>believe</i> what they do, based on the evidence of their senses and their own beliefs.<br /> <br /> Yeah, this is kind of a blatant case of &quot;belief makes you stupid&quot;, but in all honesty, it's not entirely unjustified to think &quot;hey, them doing this 'magic' causes me pain; they're not attacking me with it, so it must be coming from some one else... oh no, it must be the pain of the Earth Mother herself! Who else could it be from?&quot;<br /> <br /> I mean, I hate the Keepers for a lot of reasons, but it's not like they can actually know they're wrong. Who're they going to believe? Their own senses, or the people who, at best, dismiss their claims even as their mere presence causes a Keeper crippling agony?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5487-voiddrifter","name":"VoidDrifter","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-09T23:28:55-07:00","id":695768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VoidDrifter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/691410-compact-ride-to-damascus-the-beastcrafters?p=695429#post695429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know that. I know that. But, in universe? <b>They</b> don't know that.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's my complaint. The keepers are asking players to choose, out of charachter, to dedicate their charachter's goals to a mission they know is nonsense.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"J